<title>USA: Pearson unit buys Pyramid Research of US.</title>
<headline>Pearson unit buys Pyramid Research of US.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economist Intelligence Unit, a subsidiary of Britain's Pearson Plc, said it had bought Pyramid Research, a private U.S. telecommunications market research company.</p>
<p>In a statement released in New York on Friday, Economist Intelligence, which is part of Pearson's Economist Group, said the purchase extended its coverage &quot;to another key strategic industry,&quot; in addition to its already established automotive industry portfolio.</p>
<p>Details were not announced.</p>
<p>Revenues for the 10-year-old Pyramid, based in Massachusetts, were more than $4 million in 1996.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, (212) 859-1610))</p>
